        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c96912ff-65f0-5cf6-82d1-824d88fb598a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: British intelligence agencies, Secret Intelligence Service (MI6), Security Service (MI5), Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ)\n- Places: United Kingdom, Cheltenham, The Doughnut\n- Roles: Secretary of State for Foreign and Commonwealth Affairs, Permanent Secretary\n- Concepts: signals intelligence (SIGINT), information assurance\n\nFacts:\n- The Government of the United Kingdom maintains intelligence agencies within several different government departments.\n- The three main British intelligence agencies are the Secret Intelligence Service (MI6), the Security Service (MI5), and the Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ).\n- The Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ) is a United Kingdom intelligence and security organisation responsible for providing signals intelligence and information assurance to the government and armed forces.\n- The Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ) is based in The Doughnut in the suburbs of Cheltenham.\n- The Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ) is the responsibility of the Secretary of State for Foreign and Commonwealth Affairs, but it is not part of the Foreign Office.\n- The director of the Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ) ranks as a Permanent Secretary.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fa6cf578-ebd1-5874-be96-c2e9387c46f3",
        "text": "Page: British intelligence agencies. Sentence: The Government of the United Kingdom maintains intelligence agencies within several different government departments.\nPage: British intelligence agencies. Sentence: The three main agencies are the Secret Intelligence Service (MI6), the Security Service (MI5), and the Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ).\nPage: Government Communications Headquarters. Sentence: The Government Communications Headquarters (GCHQ) is an intelligence and security organisation responsible for providing signals intelligence (SIGINT) and information assurance to the government and armed forces of the United Kingdom.\nPage: Government Communications Headquarters. Sentence: Based in \"The Doughnut\" in the suburbs of Cheltenham, GCHQ is the responsibility of the country's Secretary of State for Foreign and Commonwealth Affairs, but it is not a part of the Foreign Office and its director ranks as a Permanent Secretary.",
